$$\pi_{\G,{\Sg'}}(\cV_{\G})$$
be the representation of $\GL_{2}(F_{\Sg'})$ over $\X^{(3)}$ associated with $\cV_{\G}$ by the local Langlands correspondence in  families for $\GL_{2}(F_{{\Sg'}})$ of \cite{LLC};  let $\chi_{\H, {\rm univ}, {\Sg'}}$ be
